    <UnitTestResult executionId="73f84cc9-be3f-4dd9-9407-c6e5b70c9be7" testId="b2ae4a45-913d-7f19-b5ca-f6b345920359" testName="WebApi.Tests.Kassa.Cov_SettlementStrayVoidAbortTests.Abort_SweepsStrayCapturedPortion_ReversesIt" computerName="Svens-MacBook-Pro" duration="00:00:02.7828841" startTime="2026-08-05T00:35:21.6267780+02:00" endTime="2026-08-05T00:35:21.6267860+02:00" testType="13cdc9d9-ddb5-4fa4-a97d-d965ccfc6d4b" outcome="Passed" testListId="8c84fa94-04c1-424b-9868-57a2d4851a1d" relativeResultsDirectory="73f84cc9-be3f-4dd9-9407-c6e5b70c9be7" />
    <UnitTestResult executionId="76b216d3-0bb2-4a2e-a3b0-8a7f727c1cc8" testId="8849059d-94b6-ace8-0675-b6f66f788684" testName="WebApi.Tests.Meals.MealsInvitationIdentityBindingTests.Only_the_account_the_company_meant_ends_up_holding_the_membership" computerName="Svens-MacBook-Pro" duration="00:00:00.0010000" startTime="2026-08-05T00:36:08.2189050+02:00" endTime="2026-08-05T00:36:08.2189050+02:00" testType="13cdc9d9-ddb5-4fa4-a97d-d965ccfc6d4b" outcome="NotExecuted" testListId="8c84fa94-04c1-424b-9868-57a2d4851a1d" relativeResultsDirectory="76b216d3-0bb2-4a2e-a3b0-8a7f727c1cc8">
      <Output>
        <StdOut>OPEN RULING — Meals owner. A shared mailbox can claim another employee's invitation because the confirmed-email match does not require the address to identify ONE account (Identity's RequireUniqueEmail is unset and AspNetUsers.Email carries no unique index). Four remedies are written up — enforce address uniqueness, bind the invitation to an account id at issue, refuse an address resolving to more than one account, or require a second channel — and choosing between them changes what a company admin must type, so it is not a test's call. This fact states the property every remedy must satisfy and is unskipped the day one lands; A_shared_mailbox_colleague_can_still_take_the_membership_the_company_meant_for_someone_else fails on that same day and is what makes this skip impossible to forget.</StdOut>
      </Output>
    </UnitTestResult>
